+# Requirements: Move off is-odd
+
+Generated by Necromancer. `is-odd` is **dead**; the chosen successor is a project-owned rebuild (kind `raise`) in `src/vendor/is-odd`.
+
+## Why
+
+- Evidence: Abandoned: the latest release (3.0.1) is 8.4 years old and nothing shows it is still looked after (low OpenSSF Maintained score). (npm)
+- Evidence: The latest release (3.0.1) is 8.4 years old. (npm)
+- Evidence: OpenSSF Scorecard rates maintenance 0 out of 10. (scorecard)
+- Advisories: none.
+
+Why this successor: You can use the modulo operator to check if a number is odd. (module-replacements). A plain `n % 2 === 1` is not equivalent (see design.md), so the project owns a small module that keeps the old answers.
+
+## R1. Know how the project uses the dependency
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want a list of every way the project uses `is-odd`, so that the migration covers all of it and nothing more.
+
+- R1.1 WHEN the project is searched, THE migration SHALL list every import, require and call of `is-odd` with the exported names used.
+- R1.2 THE list SHALL be saved in the repository so reviewers can check it against the diff.
+
+Inventory (scan: 2 files scanned, 1 using `is-odd`, no warnings):
+
+| File | Use |
+| --- | --- |
+| `src/index.js` line 3 | `const isOdd = require('is-odd');` (default export, CommonJS) |
+| `src/index.js` in `seatSide(seat)` | `isOdd(seat)`, one call, one argument; `seat` is a positive integer from `seatingPlan(count)` or whatever a caller passes to `seatSide` |
+| `test/index.test.js` | No direct use. Tests `seatSide` and `seatingPlan` through `src/index.js` |
+
+## R2. Same behaviour before and after
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want proof that the project's own `isOdd` answers like `is-odd` for the way the project uses it, so that the switch is safe.
+
+- R2.1 THE project SHALL have a differential property-based test (a séance) that asks `is-odd` and the project-owned `isOdd` the same generated questions over each API in R1.1.
+- R2.2 WHEN the two answers differ, THE test SHALL fail and print the input and both answers.
+- R2.3 WHERE both throw, THE test SHALL compare the kind of error, not the message text.
+- R2.4 THE test SHALL pass with the old implementation on both sides before any code is changed.
+- R2.5 THE séance SHALL be added to the project as `seance/is-odd/seance.test.mjs`, `src/vendor/is-odd.mjs` (later `src/vendor/is-odd.js`) and `seance/is-odd/README.md` and run with `npx vitest run seance/is-odd`.
+- R2.6 THE migration SHALL handle, or record as accepted, every known difference listed in the design.
+- R2.7 WHEN `is-odd` has been removed, THE project SHALL keep a golden-file replay test that checks the new code against the recorded answers of the old package, and the live comparison SHALL skip when `is-odd` is absent.
+
+## R3. Own a small replacement
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want a small implementation of what the project uses from `is-odd`, so that the project owns that code.
+
+- R3.1 THE project SHALL contain its own dependency-free implementation of the API listed in R1.1 at `src/vendor/is-odd.js` (the project is plain CommonJS JavaScript, so no TypeScript file is added).
+- R3.2 THE implementation SHALL have example tests for edge cases found in R1.1 in addition to the séance.
+- R3.3 WHERE the licence of `is-odd` (MIT) requires attribution, THE project SHALL keep it.
+
+## R4. Remove the dead dependency
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want `is-odd` gone, so that nothing unmaintained stays in the tree.
+
+- R4.1 THE project SHALL NOT declare `is-odd` (or its transitive `is-number`) in any manifest or lockfile after the migration.
+- R4.2 THE project tests (`npm test`) and the séance SHALL pass after the migration.
+
+## R5. Safe to undo
+
+**User story.** As a maintainer, I want each step in its own commit, so that I can revert one step without losing the others.
+
+- R5.1 THE migration SHALL be made in small commits: test first, then the switch, then the removal.
