+# Séance: is-odd, raised into your own code
+
+Generated by Necromancer (recipe `is-odd`).
+
+A séance asks the old package and its replacement the same generated questions and fails on
+any different answer. Run it before you switch, and keep it while you migrate.
+
+## Files
+
+- `seance/is-odd/seance.test.mjs`: the differential property test against the original package
+- `src/vendor/is-odd.mjs`: the function your project owns from now on (no dependency)
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+npm install --save-dev vitest fast-check is-odd
+npx vitest run seance/is-odd
+```
+
+## What it compares
+
+- The boolean returned, or the error class when the call throws (never the message).
+- Inputs: integers, safe-integer edges, doubles, NaN and infinities, numeric strings, arrays, null, undefined, booleans, objects with valueOf, bigint, symbols, functions.
+
+## Known differences
+
+Found by running the séance against the real packages.
+
+| Input | Old package | Naive replacement | In the generated replacement |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `isOdd("abc")` | `throws TypeError (expected a number)` | `false (NaN % 2 is NaN, which is not 1)` | Reproduced: the replacement converts with Math.abs and checks the result, like is-odd. |
+| `isOdd(3.5)` | `throws Error ("expected an integer")` | `false` | Reproduced. |
+| `isOdd(2 ** 53)` | `throws Error ("value exceeds maximum safe integer")` | `false` | Reproduced. |
+
+## Notes
+
+- After the switch, remove is-odd (and is-number) from package.json and keep this test, with the original recorded or still installed as a dev dependency.
+
